    "description": "<p>This release maintains the interlanguage and mathematical-translation methodology sidecar as a human-readable and reproducible record of the programme's language evidence, source-body baselines, manager handoffs, and normalization workflow.</p><p><strong>Read first:</strong> <code>00_Interlanguage_Research_Method_Current_v06_20260718.pdf</code>. It explains the governing evidence distinctions and the controlled Noether Interslavic normalization completed in tranches 002A and 002B.</p><p><strong>Current result:</strong> the complete extant Noether Interslavic production corpus contains 221 Latin-script and 221 Cyrillic-script canonical TeX units. Tranche 002A changed 146 files under reviewed paired-script orthographic rules. Tranche 002B changed 92 files under exact accepted lexical rules. Both passes were idempotent. Every changed unit compiled, all resulting pages were rendered, and no machine page-quality flag was raised. The evidence package retains exact ledgers, diffs, build and render reports, visual-QA sheets, continuation state, and reusable scripts.</p><p><strong>Translation bodies:</strong> the complete editable bodies and cumulative readers are published on the Noether record <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21421049\">10.5281/zenodo.21421049</a> under concept DOI <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20412587\">10.5281/zenodo.20412587</a>. This sidecar publishes method and evidence without duplicating the full corpus.</p><p><strong>Status:</strong> this is reproducible internal normalization and artifact-quality evidence. It is not native-speaker or community certification, peer review, a critical edition, or mathematical source-fidelity certification. Held and context-sensitive terminology remains open and is documented explicitly.</p><p><strong>GitHub:</strong> corrections and improved evidence can be suggested through issues or pull requests at <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
    "additional_descriptions": [
      {
        "description": "v0.6 adds the controlled Interslavic normalization method and complete evidence for Noether tranches 002A and 002B. It does not certify language completion, terminology acceptance, native-speaker approval, translation fidelity, mathematical source fidelity, or critical-edition status.",
        "type": {
          "id": "notes",
          "title": {
            "de": "Anmerkungen",
            "en": "Notes"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  },
